{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"agent_message","text":"The profile shows the grouped call still executes active experts largely one after another; expert GEMMs account for nearly all latency, while routing is only about 40 μs. I’m testing the provided compact MoE sorter next, which can feed a single tiled kernel across all active experts and avoid those serial per-expert launches. The verified grouped implementation remains the active `run` while I validate this path."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport torch, aiter\nD='cuda';torch.manual_seed(4);T,E,Q,B=12,160,8,32\nids=torch.randint(E,(T,Q),device=D,dtype=torch.int32)\nw=torch.rand(T,Q,device=D)\nmax_len=T*Q+E*(B-1)\nst=torch.empty(max_len,device=D,dtype=torch.int32)\nsw=torch.empty(max_len,device=D)\nse=torch.empty((max_len+B-1)//B,device=D,dtype=torch.int32)\nnv=torch.empty(1,device=D,dtype=torch.int32)\nbuf=torch.empty(E,device=D,dtype=torch.int32)\ntry:\n aiter.moe_sorting_fwd(ids,w,st,sw,se,nv,buf,E,B)\n torch.cuda.synchronize()\n n=int(nv.item())\n print('valid padded',n,'max',max_len)\n print('token ids',st[:n].cpu().tolist())\n print('expert blocks',se[:(n+B-1)//B].cpu().tolist())\n print('weights first',sw[:min(n,40)].cpu().tolist())\n print('orig ids flat',ids.flatten().cpu().tolist())\nexcept Exception as e:\n print(type(e).__name__,e)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
